index d4b71ad..396f957 100644
--- a/docs/drivers/adreno-metal.md
+++ b/docs/drivers/adreno-metal.md
@@ -118,3 +118,7 @@ profiling is opt-in with NATIVE_METAL_DRIVER_CPU_PROFILE=1; batch boundaries
 retain cumulative CPU nanoseconds, validity and query duration in type14.
 Type29 holds display-state fragments, type30 process/boot identity and type31
 the actual profiling policy. Hardware performance remains separately measured.
+
+Cache hits in the Darwin BO allocator reuse a completed buffer before scanning retired objects. A cache miss performs the existing retirement and retries the cache. Fence-completion cleanup uses a nonblocking lock attempt; memory-pressure release, age expiry and partial-unmap ownership retain their existing behavior. This avoids unrelated kernel fence/free calls on the allocation hit path.
+
+Released owned buffer backing participates in the existing bounded spare cache. Both pooled and dedicated allocations take an eligible spare before another Vulkan allocation, while retaining its address object and the original import lifetime. The buffer spare budget stays 64 MiB and expiry remains ten seconds.
